@V := "tape" :: spec [active]
  version = "1.0"

@H 1176 := "RESOURCE COMPETITION — does a scarce shared resource create the selection pressure pure mitosis lacks? (evolution MISSING #2: competition)" :: universe [🔴 CLOSED-NEG SCARCITY-BOUNDS-BUT-DOES-NOT-SELECT — F2✓ F1✗]
  seed         = "Audit gap: grep found 'competition' = 0 in the CORE engine. Selection (H_1175) only BITES when cells compete for a scarce resource (carrying capacity). Without scarcity, fitness-differential reproduction has no teeth."
  substrate    = "toy $0 CPU numpy 10 seeds. REUSE h1159b cells; ADD a scarce shared resource pool R=K_cap=6; cells draw R proportional to assignment share; when total demand (n cells) > K_cap, lowest-fitness cells (fitness=1/clustering-error) starve/die until n<=K_cap (competition). Compare COMPETITION vs unconstrained equal-survival growth. World K_true=16 >> K_cap so demand strongly exceeds supply (pre-freeze construction fix: 1st param THETA=1.6/K=8 was degenerate non-scarce — only ~9-11 cells ever born so K_cap never bit; raised K_true 8->16 + lowered THETA 1.6->0.9 + K_cap 8->6 so scarcity genuinely bites + NOCOMP runs unbounded, a_completeness_over_cheap / H_1061 defect-fix-before-score)."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (pre-reg): 🟢 COMPETITION-DRIVES-SELECTION iff F1 corr(fitness,survival)>=0.5 AND F2 COMP bounded by K_cap vs NOCOMP unbounded. 🔴 if competition does not produce fitness-tracking selection (a_paper_negative_ok)."
  result       = "🔴 SUPPORTED=FALSE (F1∧F2=F). F2 BOUNDED ✓: COMP final=6=K_cap EVERY seed, NOCOMP final=26-29 (~4.6x past K_cap, ~75 cells culled/seed) — scarcity reliably bounds population vs equal-survival runaway. F1 FITNESS-TRACKING ✗: mean corr(fit,surv)=0.303<0.5 (pooled 0.325) — POSITIVE (cull does remove lower-fitness cells) but WEAK. MECHANISM: in the clustering substrate per-cell error (fitness signal) is noisy + largely HOMOGENEOUS once cells settle near the 16 centers, so the lowest-fitness culled cells are only weakly distinguished from survivors; carrying-capacity competition is a real population BRAKE but the fitness DIFFERENTIAL is too weak for survival to TRACK fitness at corr>=0.5. Scarcity bounds, but does NOT by itself manufacture strong Darwinian selection — selection needs a real fitness differential (xref H_1175), not just scarcity."
  verdict_tier = "🔴 CLOSED-NEG (toy $0 numpy 10 seeds; scarcity=population-brake NOT selection-engine)"
  scope        = "toy; live engine + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope). p7 (fitness=clustering error, NOT perplexity)."
  artifact     = "UNIVERSE/h1176_resource_competition.py · .verdicts/1176_resource_competition/H_1176.txt"
  xref         = "1175_fitness_selection · 1171_apoptosis_death · 1172_metabolism_energy_budget · h1159b_mitosis_capacity_self_tuning"
